.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Spring target smoothing and recoil impulses\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Keeps position and velocity independently of a \fBSprite\fP\&. Call \fBupdate()\fP with a target and elapsed seconds to smooth motion, or \fBapplyImpulse()\fP to produce recoil\&. \fBgetState()\fP returns a copy; \fBsetState()\fP replaces all position and velocity fields\&.

.PP
The helper does not update automatically\&. Apply each sample to a freshly evaluated pose instead of adding it repeatedly to the previous final pose\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBAnimationSpringTarget()\fP, \fBupdate()\fP, \fBAnimation target adapters\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "AnimationSpringTarget (number mass = \fR1\fP, number stiffness = \fR100\fP, number damping = \fR20\fP)"

.PP
Create a damped spring target\&. Starts with zero position and velocity\&. The helper owns its state independently of Sprites and does not update automatically\&. All inputs must be finite\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImass\fP Positive mass; default 1\&. 
.br
\fIstiffness\fP Nonnegative restoring spring coefficient; default 100\&. 
.br
\fIdamping\fP Nonnegative damping coefficient; default 20\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const recoil = new pdg\&.AnimationSpringTarget(1, 100, 20);
recoil\&.applyImpulse(\-2, 0);
const offset = recoil\&.update(0, 0, 1 / 60);
// Apply offset\&.x/y to a freshly sampled pose\&.

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBupdate()\fP, \fBapplyImpulse()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "applyImpulse (number x, number y)"

.PP
Change spring velocity immediately\&. Each velocity component increases by impulse divided by mass\&. Position remains unchanged\&. Invalid or overflowing results leave state unchanged\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP Finite horizontal impulse in mass times distance per second\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP Finite vertical impulse in mass times distance per second\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBupdate()\fP, \fBgetState()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "object getState ()"

.PP
Copy spring position and velocity\&. Editing the returned object does not change the helper\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An independent state object described below\&.
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBSpring state\fP
.RS 4
Field  Meaning  \fRx\fP, \fRy\fP  Position in the application's chosen coordinate frame\&.  \fRvelocityX\fP, \fRvelocityY\fP  Velocity in that frame's distance units per second\&.  
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetState()\fP, \fBupdate()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "setState (object state)"

.PP
Replace spring position and velocity\&. Validates all components before changing the state\&. Invalid or overflowing values leave it unchanged\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstate\fP Object with finite x, y, velocityX, and velocityY fields; see \fBanimation_spring_state\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetState()\fP, \fBapplyImpulse()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "object update (number targetX, number targetY, number deltaSeconds)"

.PP
Advance the spring toward a fixed target\&. Uses analytic damped-spring integration, treating the target as constant throughout this step\&. Zero elapsed time preserves state\&. Invalid or overflowing results leave state unchanged\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItargetX\fP Finite target x in the same frame as the spring state\&. 
.br
\fItargetY\fP Finite target y in the same frame as the spring state\&. 
.br
\fIdeltaSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative elapsed time in seconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An owned copy of the new state; see \fBanimation_spring_state\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBgetState()\fP, \fBapplyImpulse()\fP 
.RE
.PP


